Looking at this FDTD-2D stencil, I'll apply tiling by staging rows into local buffers. The key data reuse here is in the row-neighbor accesses (`hz[i-1][j]`, `ex[i][j-1]`, `ey[i+1][j]`). I'll tile along columns (NY) for each phase, buffering the relevant rows/columns locally.

Since NY=80 and NX=60 are modest, I'll buffer full rows into local arrays for compute, separating load/compute/store phases per time step.

